   "body": "Adversarial review (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:\n\nAdversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVE at 7309cad346a8b377b76b3d7870322bebe74656b7\n\nNo security finding. Every HFR-PROTOCOL claim I could test against `R57d`-`R57k` holds.\n\n1. **Low**, `docs/lots/LOT-057-rest-browsing.md:93,115`: the spec still lists page 2, `results_per_page`, the `/api/` href and the error answer as pending capture (#355). Update the pending list in this PR, as #554 did for #335.\n2. **Low**, merge order: this branch conflicts with #873 (`MANIFEST.md`, `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md`) and with #872 (`docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md`, the E1 row). Whichever merges later needs a hand resolution, so its APPROVE does not carry over (AGENTS §8).\n3. **Detail**, `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` \"Errors\": `Cache-Control: no-transform` is not recorded in any published meta. Mark it a run observation.\n\n**Verified**\n- `anonymize.py check --corpus`: 707 of 707 clean.\n- `unittest discover tooling/fixtures/tests` (includes the manifest check): 398 OK.\n- `swift test` on HFRKit: 1992 passed.\n- markdownlint, `fold.py --check`, `check-lot-deps.py`: clean.\n- Own JSON walk of `R57d`-`R57k`: every `author` / `last_author` title is `userN`, every `tns3` is `mesdiscussions-91NNNN`, every href is a forum `/api/` href, no unexpected string key.\n- Paging claims recomputed: 5 sticky + 25 on page 1; 25 and no sticky on page 2; same `results_count` 93442; no topic on both pages; dates descending; `R57f`'s 50 are exactly `R57d` + `R57e`; ⌈93442 / 25⌉ + 1 = 3739.\n\ncloud/orch: merged now. Findings 1 and 3 (Low, spec pending list and a meta note) are left to the LOT-057 lot PR, which rewrites those lines anyway.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
